          "text": "The pattern is consistent with an **orthorhombic, ordered-rocksalt-derived structure**, indexed with approximately\n\n\\[\na=9.762\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad b=5.049\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad c=5.280\\ \\text{\u00c5}.\n\\]\n\nThe strong 18.16\u00b0 line and its harmonic near 36.80\u00b0 index as 200/400. The peaks near 33.93\u00b0 and 35.53\u00b0 correspond to 002 and 020. A **Pnma, Z = 4** model accounts for the remaining peak clusters.\n\nLi positions and the Mn/Co ordering cannot be determined very accurately from Cu X-ray powder data alone: Li scatters weakly, while Mn and Co have similar X-ray scattering factors. Thus, the coordinates below should be treated as a prototype-constrained average model suitable as a starting point for Rietveld refinement, rather than a definitive single-crystal solution.\n\n### Primary CIF\n\n```cif\ndata_Li2MnCoO4_orthorhombic\n_audit_creation_method\n'Powder indexing and ordered-rocksalt prototype assignment'\n_chemical_name_common                 'lithium manganese cobalt oxide'\n_chemical_formula_sum                 'Li8 Mn4 Co4 O16'\n_chemical_formula_structural          'Li2MnCoO4'\n_cell_formula_units_Z                 4\n\n_cell_length_a                        9.7622\n_cell_length_b                        5.0494\n_cell_length_c                        5.2800\n_cell_angle_alpha                     90\n_cell_angle_beta                      90\n_cell_angle_gamma                     90\n_cell_volume                          260.22\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt             'P n m a'\n_space_group_IT_number                62\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '1/2-x,-y,1/2+z'\n3  '-x,1/2+y,-z'\n4  '1/2+x,1/2-y,1/2-z'\n5  '-x,-y,-z'\n6  '1/2+x,y,1/2-z'\n7  'x,1/2-y,z'\n8  '1/2-x,1/2+y,1/2+z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nLi1 Li 8 d  0.0040  0.0350  0.2470  1.0  1.20\nMn1 Mn 4 c  0.2430  0.2500  0.0180  1.0  0.50\nCo1 Co 4 c  0.2580  0.2500  0.4780  1.0  0.50\nO1  O  8 d  0.1190  0.0410  0.0300  1.0  0.70\nO2  O  8 d  0.3820  0.4620  0.4700  1.0  0.70\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing is:\n\n| Observed 2\u03b8 | Principal assignment |\n|---:|:---|\n| 18.16\u00b0 | 200 |\n| 33.93\u00b0 | 002 |\n| 35.53\u00b0 | 020 |\n| 36.5\u201337.3\u00b0 | 400, 120, 311 cluster |\n| 40.84\u00b0 | 401/410 |\n| 43.14\u00b0 | 212/221 |\n| 44.62\u00b0 | 411 |\n| 54.29\u00b0 | 412 |\n| 56.53\u00b0 | 600 |\n\nThe main surviving ambiguity is **Mn/Co interchange between the two 4c sites**. That alternative has essentially the same powder peak positions and only small intensity differences with Cu K\u03b1 radiation; anomalous X-ray or neutron diffraction would be needed to distinguish it reliably.",
